/P 116 0 R
/E (The project "Arduino-Based Real-Time Sound Signal Monitoring and Analysis Using MAX4466 Microphone Module" is designed to monitor sound and display its electrical signal in real time.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
179 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 116 0 R
/E (Sound is a form of energy that travels through the air in the form of waves. The MAX4466 microphone module detects sound and converts it into an analog electrical signal. Arduino UNO reads this signal through its analog input pin.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
180 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 116 0 R
/E (The collected signal values are sent to a computer through a USB connection. The Arduino IDE Serial Plotter is used to display these values in the form of a real-time graph.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
181 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 116 0 R
/E (When a person speaks, claps or produces any other sound near the microphone, the graph changes according to the variations in the microphone signal.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
